The XML files in testdata/ (except MANIFEST.json) are copied unmodified from
the W3C XML Signature 1.1 Interop Test Report, Oracle test vectors:

  XML Signature 1.1 Interop Test Report
  https://www.w3.org/TR/2012/NOTE-xmldsig-core1-interop-20121113/
  Status: W3C Working Group Note, 13 November 2012
  Vectors: https://www.w3.org/TR/2012/NOTE-xmldsig-core1-interop-20121113/interop/xmldsig11/oracle/

The files in testdata/xmlenc11/ are from the W3C XML Encryption 1.1 Interop
Test Report, Oracle test vectors, fetched 2026-09-26:

  XML Encryption 1.1 Interop Test Report
  https://www.w3.org/TR/2012/NOTE-xmlenc-core1-interop-20121113/
  Status: W3C Working Group Note, 13 November 2012
  Vectors: https://www.w3.org/TR/2012/NOTE-xmlenc-core1-interop-20121113/files/oracle/

The .xml and .p12 files there are copied unmodified. Each .key.pem is the
private key of the .p12 of the same name (password "passwd"), extracted
with OpenSSL and re-encoded as unencrypted PKCS #8, because the Go standard
library does not read PKCS #12. They are published test keys and protect
nothing.

